      "body": "The loop condition `i < points.length` lets `i` reach the last index, where `points[i + 1]` is `undefined`. The `!` assertion hides the type error, but at runtime accessing `.x`/`.y` on `undefined` throws, crashing `polylineLength()` and the pencil hit detection for any polyline with at least one segment. It should be `i < points.length - 1`, matching the loop it replaced.\n\nSuggested fix (model-generated, not tested):\n```suggestion\n  for (let i = 0; i < points.length - 1; i++) {\n```",
